  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Salicylaldehyde is prepared by heating phenol and chloroform together in the presence of potassium hydroxide or sodium hydroxide. This reaction is called the Reimer-Tiemann reaction.</p><p>The Reimer Tiemann reaction is an organic chemical reaction where phenol is converted into an ortho hydroxy benzaldehyde using chloroform, a base, and an acid workup. This reaction can also be described as the chemical reaction used for the ortho-formylation of phenols.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0030_3b621a7cf4e5.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 146px;\"/></p></blockquote>"
